# Line-ending policy.
#
# This repo is developed on Windows (core.autocrlf=true is common) but runs in
# Linux containers. Two things break without explicit rules:

# 1. Shell scripts checked out with CRLF fail inside the container with
#    "$'\r': command not found". The dev container bootstrap is a .sh file, so
#    this would break a fresh clone's first "Reopen in Container".
*.sh            text eol=lf
*.bash          text eol=lf

# 2. static/app/ holds committed `vite build` output. Line-ending conversion
#    makes every in-container build show these bundles as modified even when
#    the bytes are identical. Treat them as opaque.
static/app/**   -text

# Other container-consumed files that must stay LF.
Dockerfile*     text eol=lf
*.yml           text eol=lf
*.yaml          text eol=lf
